From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: async reader output settings, source state, hooks, start positions, default allocator

Stubs (E_NOTIMPL / FIXME), as documented now.

- IWMReaderAdvanced2::GetOutputSetting / SetOutputSetting: the sixteen
  documented settings, per output, with the answers an audio and a video
  output give (E_INVALIDARG for a setting the output kind does not have,
  NS_E_INVALID_REQUEST for the ones that cannot be read, write-only
  DedicatedDeliveryThread, the defaults such as SoftwareScaling TRUE and
  DynamicRangeControl/SpeakerConfig -1). The table is the one Wine's
  conformance test records from native; the test no longer marks it
  todo_wine, and maps its audio=0/video=1 output numbers to the outputs by
  media type, since this file's outputs are enumerated the other way round in
  Wine. E_UNEXPECTED before Open, a wrong type or size is E_INVALIDARG, the
  value getter follows the usual length protocol.
- Source state of a file reader: GetBufferProgress (100 %, nothing buffering),
  GetDownloadProgress (100 %, the size of the file or stream), GetProtocolName
  ("file"), GetURL, CanSaveFileAs (FALSE), SaveFileAs and CancelSaveFileAs
  (NS_E_INVALID_REQUEST: only streamed content can be saved), GetSaveAsProgress,
  Preroll / StopBuffering / StopNetStreaming (S_OK once open),
  IsUsingFastCache (FALSE), GetMaxSpeedFactor (1). E_UNEXPECTED before Open.
- GetMaxOutputSampleSize (the largest sample of the output's stream),
  GetLanguageCount / GetLanguage (from the reader's language list, 0 when it
  has none; the output number is checked), SetPlayerHook (kept per output,
  released by Close), StartAtMarker (through the header's markers) and
  StartAtPosition for the 100 ns formats.
- The reader's sample allocator (AllocateForStreamEx / AllocateForOutputEx),
  which was E_NOTIMPL when the program's callback has no
  IWMReaderCallbackAdvanced, now hands out buffers of its own.

